<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">campwatch</ansi>

Camp Watch is a warrior's and a samurai's skill. Camping in the wilds is not always
safe: on the Old Kings Road, a camp rest has a 15% chance of drawing a
pair of road brigands, who come partway through the rest (between 30%
and 70% of it).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What the watch does</ansi>

  The company's best watch spots the raiders with a 25% chance per
  level (every time at level 4). Spotted, the company is roused and
  fights them, and the rest still counts: Rested, Forage, and Vigil as
  usual. Unspotted, they fall on a sleeping camp: you still fight them,
  Fatigue still recovers, but nobody is Rested and there is no Forage
  or Vigil from that rest.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Watch duty</ansi>

  Any member can also take the watch duty (<ansi fg="command">camp duties [member] watch</ansi>,
  <ansi fg="command">help camp duties</ansi>). Every watcher adds a chance of their own, their Camp
  Watch level at 25% a level and never less than 20%, and they stack with
  each other and with the specialist: two watchers spot raiders more often
  than one. The chance that at least one of them spots the raiders is the
  chance the camp has. A watcher stays up, so misses the Rested buff and
  ends the rest no better than Ready.

Camp bells and trip lines (<ansi fg="command">help camp gear</ansi>) spot raiders too: with no watch
posted they give a flat 20% chance, and with a watch they add 10 points to
its chance, up to 90%. A rest uses them a little, and after ten rests they
are spent. They also keep thieves out of a resting camp (<ansi fg="command">help camp gear</ansi>); a
posted watch gets the same chance to catch thieves as it has to spot raiders.

Watch incense (<ansi fg="command">help camp supplies</ansi>), burned for a rest, adds 10 points to a posted
watch's chance, up to 90%; a watch that already spots them every time keeps it.

Whether raiders come, and when, is settled as the rest begins, so a server
restart never rolls it again. Logging out doesn't dodge them: raiders
who find a camp with its leader gone spoil the rest the same way. If
the leader falls or leaves, any raiders still standing slip away rather
than turn on other travellers.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help specialists</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.

A successful watch also prevents enemy surprise in the raid. A missed watch may still leave time for a perceptive companion to prevent combat surprise, but the rest stays spoiled. See help ambush.
